 Photoplethysmography (rPPG) works by detecting micro-color variations in human skin caused by blood circulation. Every time the heart pumps, blood volume in facial capillaries fluctuates, altering the amount of light absorbed and reflected—particularly in the green wavelength spectrum.  Here is an end-to-end blueprint to build this project from scratch using Python, OpenCV, MediaPipe, and SciPy.1. System Architecture
